# Fixtures the native target does not run as the Wasm host does (scripts/native-checked.py).
# PATH KIND TEXT: each is checked to fail as its line says, in both builds, and never counts as passed
# (`skipped` is not built or run at all).
arithmetic/array-index-order.wy differs `a[bump(&mut a)]` reads the array after the index has changed it on native (line 3 is 70, not 41): a difference between the targets to be decided, not checked mode's
arithmetic/array-large-frame.refused.wy accepted the 1024-byte stack is the Wasm build's
arithmetic/unused-locals.refused.wy accepted the 256 scalar locals are the Wasm emitter's limit
arithmetic/unused-parameters.refused.wy accepted the 32 scalar parameters are the Wasm emitter's limit
bulk-copy/extend-from-slice-no-room.wy differs the heap that is full is the Wasm build's; on native there is room
bulk-copy/full-heap-room.wy killed SIGSEGV (the program fills the heap; on native that ends in a fault in both builds, where the Wasm heap is full and says so: to be looked at)
